  "description": "ADR-0062: an IDuplexPipe over an already-open System.IO.Ports.SerialPort, with the\n      synchronous-read-pump-on-a-dedicated-thread design that a live board on the bench proved\n      necessary — Windows' SerialPort.BaseStream.ReadAsync honours neither cancellation\n      (dotnet/runtime#30850) nor ReadTimeout, so an async pipe reader over it can hang forever on a\n      port that goes genuinely silent. Zero third-party dependency: System.IO.Ports and\n      System.IO.Pipelines only. See Periphery.Serial.Rjcp for the third-party-backed\n      alternative.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
